      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `parse_args()` has two argument-parsing bugs and repeated per-branch boilerplate in the `while` loop:\n\n1. **Flags after the positional filename are silently ignored (`*)` branch, lines 135–138):** Because `*)` runs `POSITIONAL_ARGS+\u003d(\"$@\")` and `break`s out of the loop, passing any flag after the positional `[ec.bin]` argument (e.g. `flash_fp_mcu dump.bin -r`, `flash_fp_mcu ec.bin -H`, or `flash_fp_mcu ec.bin --noservices`) stops option parsing on the filename and appends the trailing flags to `POSITIONAL_ARGS`, where `main()` silently ignores `$2`+. As a result, `flash_fp_mcu dump.bin -r` leaves `FLAGS_read` as `FLAGS_FALSE` and **writes/flashes** `dump.bin` to the MCU instead of reading from it, `flash_fp_mcu ec.bin -H` flashes the MCU instead of only pinging the bootloader, and `flash_fp_mcu ec.bin --unknown-flag` silently succeeds. `*)` should only record the current positional token (`POSITIONAL_ARGS+\u003d(\"$1\")`) and continue the loop, leaving `--)` as the explicit end-of-options delimiter.\n2. **Missing integer validation on `-R`/`--retries` and `-B`/`--baudrate` (lines 81–104):** Unlike `DEFINE_integer` in `shflags`, `parse_args()` accepts empty values (`--retries\u003d`, `--baudrate\u003d`), non-numeric strings (`--retries\u003dabc`, `-R ec.bin`), and missing values followed by another flag (`-R -r` or `-B -H`, where `$# -lt 2` is false and the next flag is silently consumed as the retry count or baudrate). Validating that `FLAGS_retries` and `FLAGS_baudrate` match `^[0-9]+$` catches empty values, missing values before another flag, and non-integer arguments.\n3. **Loop simplification:** Moving `shift` to the end of the `while` loop body (with one extra `shift` in the two-argument `-R|--retries` and `-B|--baudrate` arms) and checking `FLAGS_retries` and `FLAGS_baudrate` against `^[0-9]+$` at the end of the loop body eliminates 14 repeated `shift` statements and the duplicated `if [[ $# -lt 2 ]]` blocks:\n\n```bash\n  while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n    case \"$1\" in\n      -r|--read)\n        FLAGS_read\u003d\"${FLAGS_TRUE}\"\n        ;;\n      --noread)\n        FLAGS_read\u003d\"${FLAGS_FALSE}\"\n        ;;\n      -U|--remove_flash_read_protect)\n        FLAGS_remove_flash_read_protect\u003d\"${FLAGS_TRUE}\"\n        ;;\n      --noremove_flash_read_protect)\n        FLAGS_remove_flash_read_protect\u003d\"${FLAGS_FALSE}\"\n        ;;\n      -u|--remove_flash_write_protect)\n        FLAGS_remove_flash_write_protect\u003d\"${FLAGS_TRUE}\"\n        ;;\n      --noremove_flash_write_protect)\n        FLAGS_remove_flash_write_protect\u003d\"${FLAGS_FALSE}\"\n        ;;\n      -R|--retries)\n        FLAGS_retries\u003d\"${2:-}\"\n        shift\n        ;;\n      --retries\u003d*)\n        FLAGS_retries\u003d\"${1#*\u003d}\"\n        ;;\n      -B|--baudrate)\n        FLAGS_baudrate\u003d\"${2:-}\"\n        shift\n        ;;\n      --baudrate\u003d*)\n        FLAGS_baudrate\u003d\"${1#*\u003d}\"\n        ;;\n      -H|--hello)\n        FLAGS_hello\u003d\"${FLAGS_TRUE}\"\n        ;;\n      --nohello)\n        FLAGS_hello\u003d\"${FLAGS_FALSE}\"\n        ;;\n      -s|--services)\n        FLAGS_services\u003d\"${FLAGS_TRUE}\"\n        ;;\n      --noservices)\n        FLAGS_services\u003d\"${FLAGS_FALSE}\"\n        ;;\n      -h|--help)\n        usage\n        exit 0\n        ;;\n      --)\n        shift\n        POSITIONAL_ARGS+\u003d(\"$@\")\n        break\n        ;;\n      -*)\n        echo \"Unknown flag: $1\" \u003e\u00262\n        usage \u003e\u00262\n        return \"${EXIT_ARGUMENT}\"\n        ;;\n      *)\n        POSITIONAL_ARGS+\u003d(\"$1\")\n        ;;\n    esac\n    if [[ ! \"${FLAGS_retries}\" \u003d~ ^[0-9]+$ || \\\n          ! \"${FLAGS_baudrate}\" \u003d~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n      usage \u003e\u00262\n      return \"${EXIT_ARGUMENT}\"\n    fi\n    shift\n  done\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/4b4ad1f9-6eeb-43cb-865c-fe356bc6155e)",
