      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Several flag branches in `parse_args()` are either masked or untested here:\n\n1. **Masked state transitions for `--read` and `--hello`:** Because `parse_args()` resets `FLAGS_read` and `FLAGS_hello` to `${FLAGS_FALSE}` at the start of every call, passing `--read --noread` and `--hello --nohello` in the same `parse_args` invocation and asserting `${FLAGS_FALSE}` would still pass even if `--read`, `--noread`, `--hello`, and `--nohello` were all no-ops. Assert the positive long-flag state (`${FLAGS_TRUE}`) before testing the negated flags.\n2. **Missing coverage for positive protection/service flags, space-separated `--retries` / `--baudrate`, `--` with dash-prefixed filenames, and flags after positional arguments:**\n   * `-U`, `--remove_flash_read_protect`, `-u`, `--remove_flash_write_protect`, `-s`, and `--services` are never exercised (because their default is already `${FLAGS_TRUE}`, test them after their `--no*` counterparts so the state transition back to `${FLAGS_TRUE}` is verified).\n   * Space-separated `--retries \u003cN\u003e` and `--baudrate \u003cN\u003e` are not tested.\n   * In `-- custom_fw.bin`, `custom_fw.bin` does not start with `-`, so it would match `*)` even if `--)` were removed; pass a dash-prefixed filename after `--` (e.g. `-- -custom_fw.bin`) to verify that `--` stops option parsing.\n   * Test a flag following a positional argument (e.g. `parse_args ec.bin -r`) and `-h`/`--help`.\n\n```bash\n# 3. Positive long flags and space-separated --retries / --baudrate\nparse_args --read --noremove_flash_read_protect --remove_flash_read_protect \\\n  --noremove_flash_write_protect --remove_flash_write_protect \\\n  --retries 8 --baudrate 57600 --hello --noservices --services ec.bin\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_read}\" \"--read sets FLAGS_read\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_read_protect}\" \\\n  \"--remove_flash_read_protect\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_write_protect}\" \\\n  \"--remove_flash_write_protect\"\nassert_eq \"8\" \"${FLAGS_retries}\" \"--retries 8\"\nassert_eq \"57600\" \"${FLAGS_baudrate}\" \"--baudrate 57600\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_hello}\" \"--hello\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_services}\" \"--services\"\nassert_eq \"ec.bin\" \"${POSITIONAL_ARGS[0]}\" \"positional arg with long flags\"\n\n# 4. Negated boolean flags, short protection/service flags, --key\u003dvalue, and --\nparse_args --read --noread --noremove_flash_read_protect \\\n  --noremove_flash_write_protect --retries\u003d8 --baudrate\u003d57600 \\\n  --hello --nohello --noservices -- -custom_fw.bin\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_FALSE}\" \"${FLAGS_read}\" \"--noread sets FLAGS_read\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_FALSE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_read_protect}\" \\\n  \"--noremove_flash_read_protect\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_FALSE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_write_protect}\" \\\n  \"--noremove_flash_write_protect\"\nassert_eq \"8\" \"${FLAGS_retries}\" \"--retries\u003d8\"\nassert_eq \"57600\" \"${FLAGS_baudrate}\" \"--baudrate\u003d57600\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_FALSE}\" \"${FLAGS_hello}\" \"--nohello\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_FALSE}\" \"${FLAGS_services}\" \"--noservices\"\nassert_eq \"-custom_fw.bin\" \"${POSITIONAL_ARGS[0]}\" \"dash-prefixed positional arg after --\"\n\nparse_args --noremove_flash_read_protect -U --noremove_flash_write_protect -u \\\n  --noservices -s ec.bin -r\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_read_protect}\" \"-U sets flag\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_remove_flash_write_protect}\" \"-u sets flag\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_services}\" \"-s sets flag\"\nassert_eq \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \"${FLAGS_read}\" \"flag after positional arg\"\nassert_eq \"1\" \"${#POSITIONAL_ARGS[@]}\" \"positional arg count before flag\"\nassert_eq \"ec.bin\" \"${POSITIONAL_ARGS[0]}\" \"positional arg before flag\"\n\nhelp_out\u003d\"$(parse_args -h)\"\nassert_eq \"$(usage)\" \"${help_out}\" \"-h outputs usage and