      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Extract a small helper function with a `local` return-code variable to eliminate the repeated 4-line `ret\u003d0; parse_args ... || ret\u003d$?; assert_eq ...` boilerplate, and add test cases for `--retries`, `--baudrate`, empty `--retries\u003d` / `--baudrate\u003d`, non-integer arguments, and missing values followed by another flag:\n\n```bash\n# Error handling: unknown flag, missing values, and non-integer values\nassert_parse_err() {\n  local ret\u003d0\n  parse_args \"$@\" 2\u003e/dev/null || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"${EXIT_ARGUMENT}\" \"${ret}\" \"expected EXIT_ARGUMENT for: $*\"\n}\n\nassert_parse_err --unknown-flag\nassert_parse_err -R\nassert_parse_err --retries\nassert_parse_err --retries\u003d\nassert_parse_err --retries\u003dabc\nassert_parse_err -R abc\nassert_parse_err -R -r\nassert_parse_err -B\nassert_parse_err --baudrate\nassert_parse_err --baudrate\u003d\nassert_parse_err --baudrate\u003dabc\nassert_parse_err -B abc\nassert_parse_err -B -H\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/4b4ad1f9-6eeb-43cb-865c-fe356bc6155e)",
